<title>CHINA: Moulin Int'l year net rises 61 percent.</title>
<headline>Moulin Int'l year net rises 61 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   29.0    vs  20.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    8.0     vs  6.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil     vs  nil</p>
<p>    Net			    130.03  vs  80.71</p>
<p>    Turnover		     500.93  vs  370.62</p>
<p>    Company name		 Moulin International Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  August 28 to September 4</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   October 17</p>
<p>NOTE - Moulin International is an optical products maker.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of five-for-two shares and one warrant for every 12 shares held.</p>
<p>Each bonus warrant will confer upon its holder the right to subscribe at HK$6.50 in cash, subject to adjustments, for one new share at an initial subscription of HK$6.50 per share in the issued capital of the company at any time within two years from the issue date.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 13 H.K. cents (including an interim dividend of five cents) vs 9.2 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
